<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">31 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 31 October, from 475 to 2011.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">475 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,551 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Romulus Augustulus is proclaimed western Roman emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orestes-roman-general">Orestes</a> installed his young son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romulus">Romulus</a> as emperor in the West. Less than a year later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a> deposed him, an event conventionally taken as the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-roman-empire">Western Roman Empire</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-roman-empire">Western Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus">Romulus Augustulus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/683">683 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,343 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Kaaba is damaged by fire during the siege of Mecca</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">During the Umayyad siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a>, held by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-allah-ibn-al-zubayr">Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazid-i">Yazid I</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaaba">Kaaba</a> was severely damaged by fire. Ibn al-Zubayr later rebuilt it to include the hatīm.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaaba">Kaaba</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">802 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,224 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Empress Irene is deposed and Nikephoros I takes the throne</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Irene of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>, sole ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> since 797, was overthrown by her General Logothete, Nikephoros, who seized the throne; she was banished to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lesbos">Lesbos</a>. Her five years of sole rule had been unprecedented in Roman and Byzantine history.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikephoros-i">Nikephoros I</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lesbos">Lesbos</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1517">1517 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">509 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Martin Luther issues his Ninety-five Theses</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a> sent his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ninety-five-theses">Ninety-five Theses</a> against the sale of indulgences to the Archbishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a> and, by tradition, posted them on the church door at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wittenberg">Wittenberg</a>. The debate they sparked became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1864">1864 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">162 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nevada becomes the 36th US state</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nevada">Nevada</a> was admitted to the Union during the Civil War, with Republicans keen on its votes for Lincoln's re-election and support for the 13th Amendment. It is still called the 'Battle Born State'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1956">1956 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">70 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Britain and France begin bombing Egypt over Suez</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British and French aircraft attacked Egyptian airfields after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> rejected their ultimatum to withdraw from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suez-canal">Suez Canal</a> zone. US and Soviet pressure forced a humiliating withdrawal.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1984">1984 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">42 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Indira Gandhi is assassinated by her bodyguards</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Two <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> bodyguards shot Prime Minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indira-gandhi">Indira Gandhi</a> in her <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> garden, months after she ordered the army into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-temple">Golden Temple</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amritsar">Amritsar</a>. Anti-Sikh violence that followed killed about 3,000 people.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-temple">Golden Temple</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amritsar">Amritsar</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2011">2011 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">15 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">World population reaches seven billion, UN estimates</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> designated 31 October 2011 as the symbolic day the world's population reached seven billion. The total had doubled since the late 1960s.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a></div></div></li></ol>
